<%
# ============================================================================
# MISSION 2: RANSOMED TRUST - SCENARIO FILE
# ============================================================================
# Break Escape - Season 1: The Architect's Shadow
#
# Hospital ransomware crisis. 47 patients on life support. Exploit ENTROPY's
# backdoor to recover decryption keys before critical systems fail.
#
# ENTROPY Cell: Ransomware Incorporated
# Mission Type: Crisis Response / Recovery
# Difficulty: Beginner (Mission 2)
#
# CORE PREMISE (why a "legitimate" consultant still has to work for every door):
#   The ransomware encrypted the hospital's access control server along with
#   everything else. Nobody in this building can GRANT access any more -- the
#   system that issues permissions is itself behind the ransom screen. So the
#   player's consultant cover buys goodwill and a paper visitor badge, and
#   nothing else. Every restricted door now needs a PERSON to open it, a
#   mechanical override key, or a pick. That is the mission.
#
# NARRATIVE SPINE (gated story beats):
#   ACT I   Talk your way past the desk. Bernie Nwosu holds the IT override key
#           and will not hand it to a stranger. Social engineering or picks.
#   ACT II  Gary Whitlock holds the only working reader-card in the building.
#           Four routes to it: rapport, leverage, theft, force.
#   TURN    THE COVER BURNS. Someone phones security and pulls the player's
#           booking. The consultant line stops working. Freedom of movement
#           must be re-earned -- and WHO made that call is the intrigue.
#   ACT III The backup server. VM exploitation is on the critical path: the
#           backdoor flag (Ghost's deployment log) reveals an override badge
#           held the drill doors, Ghost's log (flag 4) names the badge, and the
#           press relay refuses to authenticate without the full flag set.
#   ACT IV  Four decisions that all pay back in the debrief.
#
# NEW MECHANICS (over m01):
# - Cover-burn state change mid-mission (guard behaviour + dialogue both branch)
# - Social-engineering gate with multiple redundant routes (no soft-locks)
# - PIN safe cracking (4-digit puzzle) + ENTROPY keypad oracle (Mastermind-style info-leak), lockpick-gated in a sealed case
# - Flag-locked container (VM progress unlocks physical loot)
# - Moral dilemma interface (ransom decision)
# - Ransomware display minigame (infected terminals)
# - Backup recovery minigame (restore hospital systems), fed by flag rewards:
#   flag 3 pays out a Verified Restore Manifest (no restore of any kind without
#   it) and flag 4 opens the staging cache holding Ghost's key material (the
#   four-hour combined restore)
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (verified overlap-free by scripts/validate_scenario.rb):
#
#                                      [CTO Office]
#                                      (open, Kim)
#                                           |
#               [Boardroom]---------[Night Handover]---------[IT Department]
#               (locked-pin)         (staff_room)             (locked-key)
#                                           |
#   [Server Room]--[Security Office]--[====== Main Corridor ======]
#    (locked-rfid)   (locked-key)      (Val patrols)  |
#                                            [Ward Link]--[==== Patient Ward ====]--[Emergency Storage]
#                                                                        |              (PIN safe)
#                          [Reception]--[Ward Vestibule]--[== Ward Approach ==]
#                            START
#
#   By id: reception_lobby -> ward_vestibule -> ward_approach -> hospital_ward
#   (+ emergency_equipment_storage east) -> ward_hall -> office_corridor ->
#   staff_room, the night handover room (dr_kim_office north, it_department east,
#   conference_room -- the Boardroom -- west). security_office sits west of the
#   corridor, and server_room west of security.
#
#   VAL'S TURNSTILE (pass 4, U2): Val Okonkwo patrols office_corridor in front of
#   the security office's key-locked door, the only way to the server room. Talk
#   her round (she opens it with #unlock_door), pick it while her back is turned
#   (lockpick_used_in_view on her), or KO her and take her key. cover_restored
#   means only "somebody accepted you" -- Bernie's vouch or Val's clearance --
#   so the COVER BURNED credit and debrief lines are reachable.
#   The three offices use their own room types: room_hospital_office_it,
#   room_hospital_office_cto and room_hospital_office_security.
#
#   DOOR SIDES (predicted from doors.js placement maths, see scratchpad/doorsim.py):
#     Patient Ward  south -> RIGHT  == the player enters at the ward's BOTTOM-RIGHT.
#                                      Forced by putting Ward Approach two grid units
#                                      wide on an ODD grid column: the south-door
#                                      parity check is (gridX + gridY) % 2 on the
#                                      shared bottom wall, so the ward must sit on an
#                                      odd column for the door to take the SE corner.
#     Patient Ward  west  -> TOP    == the route on to the offices leaves from the
#                                      ward's TOP-LEFT (single E/W doors are always
#                                      placed 2.5 tiles down from the room's top).
#   Do not casually reorder these connections -- the door corners will move.
# ============================================================================

# ERB Helper Methods
def rot13(text)
  text.tr('A-Za-z', 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m')
end

# Narrative Content Variables
gary_warning_email = "From: Gary Whitlock (IT Systems)\nTo: Dr. Sarah Kim (CTO)\nCC: Board Secretariat\nDate: 8 November\nSubject: URGENT -- ProFTPD 1.3.3c backdoor on backup server\n\nDr Kim,\n\nSeventh time of asking. The backup server is still running ProFTPD 1.3.3c -- the trojaned source release from 2010. That build carries a backdoor in its own source code, which gives an attacker remote code execution with no credentials at all. A clean version has been available since 2010.\n\nThis box holds every clinical backup we have. If it goes, the wards go with it.\n\nI have costed the remediation at £85,000. That is the whole ask. I am not asking for a project, I am asking for a server that is not fourteen years out of date.\n\nPlease put this in front of the board as CRITICAL and not as an IT wish-list item.\n\nGary"

board_reply_email = "From: Dr. Sarah Kim (CTO)\nTo: Gary Whitlock (IT Systems)\nDate: 12 November\nSubject: RE: URGENT -- ProFTPD backdoor on backup server\n\nGary,\n\nNoted, and I do understand. The board reviewed it on Tuesday. The position is that the imaging replacement takes precedence this cycle and infrastructure security is deferred to FY25.\n\nI would ask you not to escalate this again outside the department. It does not help either of us.\n\nSarah"

recovery_instructions_encoded = rot13("SITE NOTE -- RECOVERY POSTURE. THEIR ESCROW COPY IS OFFLINE AND I CANNOT REACH IT. OFFLINE SET ALONE = 12 HOURS. OFFLINE SET PLUS MY KEY MATERIAL (CACHE, THIS RACK) = 4 HOURS. THEY WILL NOT WORK THAT OUT IN TIME, SO THEY WILL PAY.")

# Board room door code -- also written in Dr. Kim's desk diary and spoken by Kim.
boardroom_pin = "0417"
