          "observations": "A composed man in a plain suit beside the comms terminal. Hospital lanyard, no uniform, no scrubs. He nods at you the way staff nod at other staff -- and he has been on the phone recently.",
<%# Pass 4: the ambush used to fire on decide_hospital_exposure in the same pass that
    the terminal set mission_complete, so the debrief cutscene and the ambush raced.
    Now the terminal holds mission_complete back when the insider was never named and
    sets awaiting_ambush instead; the ambush ink sets mission_complete as it closes.
    The ambush is a walk-out, not a fight, so "escaped" and a KO can't both be true.
    Backstops: Reeves' start knot resumes it, the terminal's start knot completes it,
    and the room_entered mappings on closing_debrief_trigger complete it on the next
    room change. Round 2: the scene has one player reply, so it can't be closed (disableClose). %>
          "eventMappings": [
            {
              "eventPattern": "global_variable_changed:awaiting_ambush",
              "condition": "value === true && globalVars.in_conference_room === true && !globalVars.insider_identified && !globalVars.insider_confronted",
              "onceOnly": true,
              "conversationMode": "person-chat",
              "background": "assets/backgrounds/hospital1.png",
